1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers the main points. It names the fund website's daily holdings page as the starting point. It separates holdings from creation/redemption baskets (cash components, sampling, substitutions). It notes the PCF goes mainly through NSCC to authorized participants. It suggests asking the sponsor or a broker for the PCF and warns not to assume a named fund posts one. However, it wrongly says 'Rule 6c-11 generally requires daily public posting' of the PCF. Rule 6c-11 requires public disclosure of portfolio holdings, not publication of every transaction basket or PCF. This error contradicts the key distinction and suggests a public PCF is mandated. It also points to investor relations rather than the capital-markets team, a minor gap. The central content is useful, but this substantive error keeps it from full credit.\"}","ttft_ms":1889,"type":"result","duration_ms":4530,"uuid":"ff054b9a-55f3-478c-b73d-6d9558cf8273","ttft_stream_ms":545,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":545,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
